    "reading": "read the two numbers together. The predicted spread is well below the truth's, but the OLS slope of empirical on predicted sits near 1, which is what the low ECE already said: the arm is not systematically shrunk, it is noisy. Pearson is unchanged by any shared affine squash, so flatness is a description of the miss and not on its own a cause of it -- slope = r * sd(truth) / sd(predicted) ties the three together"
